> Also, small vocab question, I've seen the term "playground" used a
> lot, but am not entirely sure what it means in this context. =A0Is it
> just another term for the active version of everything?

     Yes.  The "playground" or "playground directory" is
where nethack keeps the data files for games in progress,
and is usually the same directory where nethack.exe (or
possibly nethackW.exe) is located.  Ordinarily that will
be an entirely different directory than where the source
code files are, and you would copy or move nethack.exe to
it after successfully building the program.  It is feasible
to leave nethack.exe in src and copy the processed data
files there, but you'll end up with a lot of not-very-
related files sharing a pretty big directory.


